# Walkthrough — DTO, Exception, Security, Config & Audit Implementation

We have successfully created and integrated the **DTO**, **Exception**, **Security**, **Config**, and **Audit** layers into the Spring Boot backend (`com.examly.springapp`).

---

## 1. Added & Configured Components

### 📦 DTO Layer (`com.examly.springapp.dto`)
Created clean Data Transfer Objects to isolate database entities from API contracts and handle validation:
- **[LoginRequest.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/LoginRequest.java)**: Validates email and password inputs.
- **[RegisterRequest.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/RegisterRequest.java)**: Validates name, email, 10-digit phone number, password, and role.
- **[AuthResponse.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/AuthResponse.java)**: Returns JWT bearer token, user ID, name, email, and role upon login/registration.
- **[UserDTO.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/UserDTO.java)**: Safe user representation without sensitive fields.
- **[FarmerProfileDTO.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/FarmerProfileDTO.java)**, **[PolicyDTO.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/PolicyDTO.java)**, **[LossNotificationDTO.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/LossNotificationDTO.java)**, **[SurveyAssignmentDTO.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/SurveyAssignmentDTO.java)**, **[ClaimDTO.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/ClaimDTO.java)**: Domain transfer objects.
- **[ApiResponse.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/dto/ApiResponse.java)**: Generic standard API response envelope (`success`, `message`, `data`, `timestamp`).

