### ⚠️ Custom Exception & Global Exception Handling (`com.examly.springapp.exception`)
Created custom exception classes and a centralized `@ControllerAdvice`:
- **[ResourceNotFoundException.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/exception/ResourceNotFoundException.java)**: Returns HTTP 404 Not Found.
- **[InvalidNameException.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/exception/InvalidNameException.java)** & **[InvalidPhoneException.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/exception/InvalidPhoneException.java)**: Return HTTP 400 Bad Request.
- **[DuplicateClaimException.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/exception/DuplicateClaimException.java)**: Returns HTTP 409 Conflict.
- **[UnauthorisedAccessException.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/exception/UnauthorisedAccessException.java)**: Returns HTTP 403 Forbidden.
- **[ErrorDetails.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/exception/ErrorDetails.java)**: Formats error JSON payload with timestamp, status, error, message, path, and field validation maps.
- **[GlobalExceptionHandler.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/exception/GlobalExceptionHandler.java)**: `@ControllerAdvice` mapping custom exceptions and `@Valid` validation failures to `ErrorDetails`.

---

### 🔐 Security & JWT Authentication (`com.examly.springapp.security`)
Implemented stateless authentication using Spring Security + JWT:
- **[JwtTokenProvider.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/security/JwtTokenProvider.java)**: Generates and validates HS256 JWT tokens.
- **[CustomUserDetails.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/security/CustomUserDetails.java)**: Wraps `User` entity for Spring Security context.
- **[CustomUserDetailsService.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/security/CustomUserDetailsService.java)**: Loads users by email or phone number.
- **[JwtAuthenticationFilter.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/security/JwtAuthenticationFilter.java)**: Extracts `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header, validates token, and sets security context.

---

### ⚙️ System Configuration (`com.examly.springapp.config`)
- **[SecurityConfig.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/config/SecurityConfig.java)**: Configures `BCryptPasswordEncoder`, permits `/api/auth/**`, sets stateless session creation, and adds JWT filter.
- **[CorsConfig.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/config/CorsConfig.java)**: Allows cross-origin requests from React ports (`http://localhost:8081`, `http://localhost:3000`, `http://localhost:5173`).
- **[AuditConfig.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/config/AuditConfig.java)**: Enables `@EnableJpaAuditing` and provides `AuditorAware<String>`.
- **[DataSeeder.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/config/DataSeeder.java)**: `CommandLineRunner` populating default users (`ADMIN`, `FARMER`, `INSURER`, `SURVEYOR`) with BCrypt hashed passwords when the database is empty.

---

### 🔑 Authentication Controller (`com.examly.springapp.controller`)
- **[AuthController.java](file:///d:/programming-projects/ad-project/springapp/src/main/java/com/examly/springapp/controller/AuthController.java)**: Exposes endpoints:
  - `POST /api/auth/register` — Registers user, hashes password, logs audit action, and returns `AuthResponse` with JWT token.
  - `POST /api/auth/login` — Authenticates user, updates last login, logs audit action, and returns `AuthResponse` with JWT token.

---

## 2. API Endpoints Overview

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Public / Auth |
|---|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/auth/register` | Register a new user (`FARMER`, `INSURER`, `SURVEYOR`, `ADMIN`) | Public |
| `POST` | `/api/auth/login` | Authenticate user & issue JWT token | Public |
| `GET` | `/api/users` | List all registered users | Authenticated |
| `GET` | `/api/policies` | Policy endpoints | Authenticated |
| `POST` | `/api/claims/initiate` | Claim initiation | Authenticated |
| `GET` | `/api/audit-logs` | Retrieve system audit logs | Authenticated |

